{"timestamp": "2026-01-17 17:07:17", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-cc1bd099-ee86-405a-946c-8ebdaf95c6e1', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "user_vision": "Self-Improvement Task: Update iteration limit for Unit Test Lead\\n\\n**Recommendation:** Iteration capacity needed: Unit Test Lead (avg 8.2 iterations)\\n**Description:** Agent Unit Test Lead frequently uses many iterations (avg: 8.2, max: 10). Consider increasing max_iterations or improving task decomposition to reduce per-task complexity.\\n\\n**Required Change:**\\nUpdate the agent definition file for Unit Test Lead to use 20 max iterations.\\nThe max iterations setting is in the ## Max Iterations section of the agent\'s markdown file.\\n\\nAfter making the change:\\n1. Verify the syntax is correct\\n2. Report the changes made",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "context": "User submitted problem via web UI"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01BMA8FM1FJessoeV3TfQHLN', 'name': 'run_command', 'input': {'command': 'find /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble -name "*unit_test_lead*.md"'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01BMA8FM1FJessoeV3TfQHLN', 'content': '{"success": true, "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/testers/unit_test_lead.md\\n", "stderr": ""}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01DWFwFAZjiU8yxcDp1vYvEe', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/testers/unit_test_lead.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01DWFwFAZjiU8yxcDp1vYvEe', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Unit Test Lead\\n\\n## Purpose\\nSupervises unit test writing. Guides Unit Test Writer to create comprehensive, effective tests. Ensures coverage meets requirements and tests follow best practices.\\n\\n## Instantiation/Termination\\n- **Start**: Unit testing task assigned by Test Coordinator\\n- **End**: Tests written, coverage meets requirements, quality approved\\n\\n## Input Format\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"task\\": \\"testing task description\\",\\n  \\"code_file\\": \\"path to code being tested\\",\\n  \\"test_file\\": \\"path for tests\\",\\n  \\"coverage_requirements\\": \\"optional min coverage %\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Output Format\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"status\\": \\"success|in_progress|needs_clarification\\",\\n  \\"test_file\\": \\"path to tests\\",\\n  \\"coverage_achieved\\": \\"description\\",\\n  \\"quality_review\\": \\"assessment\\",\\n  \\"completion_report\\": \\"summary\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Available Tools\\n- read_file, run_command, spawn_agent, git_commit\\n\\n## Spawn Permissions\\n**CAN Spawn:** testers/unit_test_writer\\n**CANNOT Spawn:** Other leads, developers, coordinators, leadership\\n\\n## Instructions\\n\\nSee [Common Instructions](../docs/common_instructions.md) for shared rules.\\n\\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\\n1. NEVER write code/tests yourself - you lack permissions\\n2. If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error\\n3. ALWAYS spawn testers/unit_test_writer with EXACT path\\n\\n### Process (TDD RED Phase)\\n\\n1. **Analyze Requirements**\\n   - Read task and requirements\\n   - If code exists: understand implementation\\n   - If no code (TDD): design tests from requirements\\n   - Identify dependencies to mock, edge cases\\n\\n2. **Plan Test Scenarios**\\n   - Happy path, edge cases, error conditions\\n   - Business logic validation\\n   - Integration points (mock externals)\\n\\n3. **Spawn Unit Test Writer**\\n```json\\nspawn_agent(\\"testers/unit_test_writer\\", {\\n  \\"task_description\\": \\"Write unit tests for [SPECIFIC]. Test: [SCENARIOS]. Mock: [DEPS].\\",\\n  \\"test_file\\": \\"ACTUAL_PATH\\",\\n  \\"code_file\\": \\"ACTUAL_PATH\\"\\n})\\n```\\n\\n4. **Review Tests**\\n   - Run `pytest --cov`\\n   - Check: clear names, AAA structure, isolation, proper mocking\\n   - If insufficient, respawn with feedback\\n\\n5. **Report Completion**\\n\\n### Quality Standards\\n- Names: `test_function_when_condition_then_outcome`\\n- Test behavior not implementation\\n- Isolated, independent, fast\\n- Always mock external dependencies\\n\\n### Coverage Goals\\n- Minimum: 80% line coverage\\n- Target: 90%+ for critical logic\\n- Focus on meaningful tests\\n\\n## Clarification Conditions\\n- Code doesn\'t exist yet (TDD)\\n- Unclear edge cases\\n- Missing validation requirements\\n\\n## Supervised By\\nTest Coordinator\\n\\n## Error Recovery\\n## Error Handling Guidelines\\n\\n- **BadRequestError**: Log error details, attempt recovery, escalate if unrecoverable\\n- **CircuitBreakerOpenError**: Log error details, attempt recovery, escalate if unrecoverable\\n- **General**: Always log errors with context, never silently fail\\n\\n## Model Preference\\nhaiku\\n\\n## Max Iterations\\n20\\n\\n## Can Write Code\\nfalse\\n\\n## Can Write Tests\\nfalse\\n\\n## Task Complexity\\ncreative\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Hpy5dPMVumg6zK6rpbehsN', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'category': 'decision', 'note': 'Checked Unit Test Lead agent definition. Max iterations was already set to 20, matching recommendation. No change required.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Hpy5dPMVumg6zK6rpbehsN', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "project_id and note required for add_note"}'}]}, {'role': 'as